[DONE] Make "Rooms" config on Floor Plan more user friendly. The buttons are awkward currently.
  Reworked the view-mode room controller to match the Lights-page pattern: each room is a card whose whole header (color dot + name + count) is the button that opens the room color/brightness/scene editor, with a single on/off slide switch on the right — replacing the awkward On / Off / Color… button triple and the inline scene chip row. Scenes moved into the editor as a "✦ Scenes" modal (apply any global scene to the room, or save the room's current look). Extracted SceneButton + SceneModal into components/scenes.tsx so the Lights page and Floor Plan share one implementation.

[RESEARCHED — not feasible via the public API] Support for Govee distributed gateway, if it's exposed via API.
  Findings: Govee's Developer (cloud) API v2 (/user/devices) returns a FLAT device list — there is no gateway→sub-device hierarchy exposed. Devices that sit behind a Wi-Fi gateway / are BLE-only (e.g. the H5179 thermo-hygrometer) are explicitly NOT controllable through the API: they carry flags like iot_api_supported:false, ble_only:true, lan_api_capable:false, and calls 400. The community path for those is Govee's MQTT/IoT broker or BLE — not the documented REST API, and they're sensors, not lights. Conclusion: a gateway sub-device feature can't be built as a Bifrost light provider against the public API. Left unimplemented; revisit only if Govee exposes sub-devices, or as a separate (non-light) MQTT integration.

[DONE] Support for Govee LAN API mode.
  New "govee-lan" provider (src/providers/govee_lan/mod.rs) implementing the documented Govee LAN UDP protocol: multicast scan to 239.255.255.250:4001, replies on 4002, per-device control on 4003 (turn / brightness / colorwc / devStatus). No API key — config is just the bind interface (defaults to 0.0.0.0). Registered in ProviderRegistry (the only place), so it shows up in Settings and is polled automatically (30s, since local UDP has no daily quota). RGBWW capabilities (dimmable + color + CT). Tested against a loopback mock UDP "device": discovery, devStatus parsing, unreachable-on-timeout, and turn/brightness/colorwc/CT command emission — 8 tests + a registry build test. Deployment note: needs Docker host networking for multicast to reach the LAN, and "LAN Control" enabled per-device in the Govee app.
